    "answer": {
      "short": "False. $x^0=1$ for $x\\ne0$; $0^0$ is undefined.",
      "worked": "For $x\\ne0$,$$\\begin{align*}x^0&=x^{1-1}\\\\x^0&=\\frac{x}{x}\\\\x^0&=1.\\end{align*}$$False. At $x=0$, the expression $0^0$ is undefined in this real-algebra context.",
